<h2 id="managing-the-queue-in-real-time"><a class="heading-anchor" href="#managing-the-queue-in-real-time">Managing the queue in real time</a></h2>
<p>Resolving individual tickets is only part of the job. We also need to understand what is happening across the queue. Grok Bot watches inbound volume continuously and adjusts the queue based on what needs attention. It can reprioritize tickets, reassign ownership based on urgency, and alert the organization when we are getting close to breaching a response-time SLA.</p>
<p>Grok Bot also looks across tickets for patterns. When the volume around a particular issue reaches a set threshold, it can declare an incident automatically. It monitors X for changes in sentiment and recurring reports of the same problem, giving us a view beyond the customers who contact support directly. Together, these signals help us spot emerging problems early.</p>
